#
# SMA-634. The kernel's wasm binary is a tracked binary file, and its glue is generated.
# `binary` keeps git from attempting a text diff or an end-of-line conversion, which also makes the
# Windows checkout safe without git's NUL heuristic — prebuild.yml checks the tree out on
# windows-latest.
#
# A rebase or merge conflict in these five files is NEVER resolved by hand: take either side, run
# `moon run paigasus-kernel-ts:generate-wasm`, and commit its result. The drift gate then proves
# that the five files agree with the Rust source.
#
# The four glue files carry `text eol=lf`, not `linguist-generated` alone. wasm-pack writes LF, and
# the drift gate compares the WORKING-TREE bytes against a fresh build's. A Windows developer with
# `core.autocrlf=true` would otherwise check the glue out with CRLF and red check 1 on a diff that
# means nothing about the Rust source. The binary keeps `binary`, which already implies no
# end-of-line conversion.
rs/crates/bindings/paigasus-wasm/paigasus_wasm_bg.wasm binary
rs/crates/bindings/paigasus-wasm/paigasus_wasm_bg.js text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
rs/crates/bindings/paigasus-wasm/paigasus_wasm.js text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
rs/crates/bindings/paigasus-wasm/paigasus_wasm.d.ts text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
rs/crates/bindings/paigasus-wasm/paigasus_wasm_bg.wasm.d.ts text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
